//! [config-section]
\brief Manages application configuration and lifecycle

\section1 Initialization And Startup Sequence

Use \c{QCoreApplication::instance()} to access the application singleton.
The initialization order is determined by the \l{Q_INIT_RESOURCE}{resource system}.

\section2 Platform-Specific Configuration Options

Each platform provides its own default storage location for \l{QSettings}{settings}.
Call \c{QSettings::setPath()} to override the default path on \macos or Linux.

\section1 Shutdown and cleanup

Call \c{QCoreApplication::quit()} to terminate the event loop gracefully.
All \l{QObject}{QObjects} registered with the application are destroyed on exit.

\section2 Error handling and recovery

Unhandled exceptions in the event loop cause the application to terminate.
Use \c{QApplication::notify()} to install a global exception handler.
//! [config-section]

// SHOULD NOT WARN: brief ends with period, sentence-case headings

//! [watcher-section]
\brief Provides a cross-platform file system watcher.

\section1 Monitoring files and directories

Use \c{addPath()} to register a path for monitoring.
Qt emits the \c{fileChanged()} signal when the file changes.
//! [watcher-section]
